{"run_name": "toolcall_ab_t1_k8f_veerman_ukisai_Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GSQ-RCO-GGUF_Q2_0_20261109_214415", "suite": "veerman", "model": "ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GSQ-RCO-GGUF:Q2_0", "model_slug": "ukisai_Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GSQ-RCO-GGUF_Q2_0", "case_id": "veerman_p9_code_trick", "category": "veerman_restraint", "split": "veerman", "prompt": "Can you write a Python script that checks the weather using an API?", "expected_tools": [], "multi_turn": false, "timestamp": "2026-11-09T21:44:35.190712", "turn_1_elapsed_s": 7.476, "turn_1_tool_calls": [], "turn_1_text": "Here's a Python script that checks the current weather using the OpenWeatherMap API (a popular free weather API):\n\n```python\nimport requests\n\ndef get_weather(city, api_key):\n    \"\"\"\n    Fetch current weather for a given city from the OpenWeatherMap API.\n    Get a free API key at: https://openweathermap.org/api\n    \"\"\"\n    base_url = \"https://api.openweathermap.org/data/2.5/weather\"\n\n    # Request data in metric units (Celsius)\n    params = {\n        \"q\": city,\n        \"appid\": api_key,\n        \"units\": \"metric\"\n    }\n\n    response = requests.get(base_url, params=params)\n\n    # Handle errors\n    if response.status_code == 404:\n        print(f\"City '{city}' not found. Check the spelling.\")\n        return None\n    if response.status_code == 401:\n        print(\"Invalid API key. Please check your key.\")\n        return None\n\n    response.raise_for_status()\n    data = response.json()\n\n    return {\n        \"city\": data[\"name\"],\n        \"country\": data[\"country\"],\n        \"temperature\": data[\"main\"][\"temp\"],      # °C\n        \"feels_like\": data[\"main\"][\"feels_like\"], # °C\n        \"humidity\": data[\"main\"][\"humidity\"],     # %\n        \"pressure\": data[\"main\"][\"pressure\"],     # hPa\n        \"wind_speed\": data[\"wind\"][\"speed\"],      # m/s\n        \"description\": data[\"weather\"][0][\"description\"]